  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tAccounts Production\n\t\tCommunity Interest Companies (CIC)\n\n### CIC Filings in Accounts Production\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Mon, 17 Aug, 2026 at  1:30 PM\n\n\t\tA community interest company (CIC) files a CIC 34 report alongside its annual accounts. In Capium, the annual accounts are produced exactly as they are for any other limited company client, and the CIC 34 report is prepared separately and packaged with them before filing.\n\nThis article is the overview of the process. Each step has its own article with the full detail.\n\n### \nThe CIC features in Capium\n\nOnce a client is flagged as a CIC, three features appear in Accounts Production for that client.\n\nFeatureWhere it appearsWhat it doesCIC 34 NotesSettingsHolds the content of each part of the CIC 34 reportCIC ReportsReportsGenerates the CIC 34 report from the notesCIC Submissions WizardTasksBuilds the zip package and links through to Companies House\nNone of these appear until the CIC option is ticked against the client.\n\n### The process in order\n\nStepWhat you doArticle1Flag the client as a CICEnabling the CIC option for a client2Produce the annual accounts as normalHow to prepare a set of Accounts3Complete the CIC 34 NotesCompleting the CIC 34 Notes4Generate the CIC 34 reportGenerating the CIC 34 report5Build the zip packageCreating the CIC submission package6File and record the submissionFiling the CIC package with Companies HouseSteps 2 and 3 can be done in either order, but both must be finished before step 5, because the wizard needs a generated accounts report and a generated CIC report to build the package.\n\n### \nPoints to be aware of\n\nThe accounts side of the process is unchanged. Accounting periods, trial balance, report settings and annual accounts all work as they do for any limited company client.\nThe CIC 34 report covers the current financial year only. There is no comparative column and no prior year content to complete.\nNothing in the CIC 34 Notes is populated automatically. Every part is entered manually for each client, each year.\nThere is no direct or API submission for CIC filings. Capium prepares and packages the reports, and the upload and payment take place on the Companies House website.\n\n### \nRelated articles\n\nEnabling the CIC option for a client\nCompleting the CIC 34 Notes\nGenerating the CIC 34 report\nCreating the CIC submission package\nFiling the CIC package with Companies House\nHow to prepare a set of Accounts\nAdd Accounting Periods\nHow to add Trial Balance\nReport Settings in Accounts\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
